Pedro Pathing Visualizer - BIOBUZZ Edition
Copyright 2026 MartinMax0711

This edition is based on Pedro Pathing Visualizer
(https://github.com/Pedro-Pathing/Visualizer) at upstream commit f54357e
(f54357e9bcd20d28fd0ee32df8e89573a8f9c12c), licensed under the Apache License
2.0, and is distributed under the same license (see LICENSE). It adapts the
upstream sources for the FIRST Tech Challenge 2026-2027 BIOBUZZ season: a
BIOBUZZ field model and field artwork, fixed field obstacles, starting-pose
presets and legality checks, alliance rotation, collision warnings, Pedro
Pathing 2.x code export fixes, GitHub Pages deployment, a team library mode
used when the Huskyteers Portal serves the planner at /planner/, and related
user-interface changes.

Modified files: each source file taken from upstream and changed for this
edition carries a short "Modified for the BIOBUZZ Edition" comment at the top.
Changed upstream files that cannot hold a comment are package.json,
package-lock.json and public/favicon.ico. README.md and this NOTICE were
rewritten for this edition.

Added files (new in this edition, not part of upstream):

  .github/workflows/deploy.yml
  public/fields/biobuzz.svg
  public/icons/* (apple-touch-icon.png, icon.svg, icon-192.png,
    icon-512.png, icon-maskable-512.png)
  public/manifest.webmanifest
  public/theme.js (the saved theme before first paint, formerly inline in
    index.html)
  scripts/generate-biobuzz-field.ts
  scripts/third-party-licenses.mjs, third-party-licenses.d.mts (writes
    THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt into each build)
  src/biobuzz/* (field model, start-pose rules, alliance rotation, collision
    sweep)
  src/lib/components/BiobuzzOverlay.svelte
  src/lib/components/LibraryBrowser.svelte, LibraryConflictDialog.svelte,
    LibraryNotice.svelte, LibrarySaveDialog.svelte (team library UI)
  src/utils/assets.ts
  src/utils/portalLibrary.ts, portalMode.ts, teamLibrary.ts,
    libraryFormat.ts, toast.ts (team library)
  tests: src/biobuzz/__tests__/*, src/utils/__tests__/*

Third-party software bundled into the built app (d3, Svelte, lodash, two.js,
gif.js, html2canvas, highlight.js, hotkeys-js, prettier, prettier-plugin-java,
chevrotain and others) is listed, with each package's license and notice
files, in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt next to index.html in every build.

